  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:filter-bubble",
  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "A state of informational isolation in which algorithmic personalisation \u2014 recommendation systems, personalised search, and engagement-optimised feeds \u2014 progressively narrows the content a person encounters to material predicted to match their existing preferences and beliefs, reducing exposure to disconfirming viewpoints without the person's awareness or consent; coined by Eli Pariser in 2011, the concept names a structural harm of personalised media that feeds polarisation, reinforces bias, and erodes the shared factual ground of public discourse.",
